# Git treated README.md as binary, permanently.
#
# The original README in the first commit had a stray UTF-16 fragment appended.
# Git sniffs content, decided the file was binary, and from then on every diff
# and merge of it said "Binary files differ" instead of showing lines — so a
# one-character edit on GitHub produced a merge conflict nobody could read or
# resolve.
#
# The file itself is fine now, but Git re-derives the binary flag per blob, so
# this needs pinning explicitly. Without it the same trap reappears the next time
# an editor saves the file with an unexpected encoding.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.md   text
*.ts   text
*.tsx  text
*.js   text
*.mjs  text
*.mts  text
*.json text
*.sql  text
*.css  text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text

# Images are binary, whatever the content sniffer decides.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text